{
  "$description": "Piconet's look, direction D, described once: every colour, size and motion value the launcher (Theme.axaml), the runner's game window (overlay.h), the site (global.css) and the service's pages share. The Design Tokens Community Group's format, as Style Dictionary reads it: groups, $type, $value, {group.token} aliases. generate.py writes it out as generated/Theme.g.axaml (the launcher's resources), generated/theme_palette.g.h (the runner's palette) and generated/theme.g.css (the site's and the service's custom properties): theme.py says how each is named. A value changed here changes everywhere; nothing else types one.",
  "color": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$description": "The colours by role. Tones, not strokes: ground (the window), column (the left column), well (a panel, a card, a tile, an input's ground), raised (a plate on a surface, a surface button), hover (one tone up). White on black: text is white, dim and faint are the secondary greys (each passes 4.5:1 on every tone). The accent (green) is what is yours or active and may fill, with on-accent text on it; gold is the mark only, never a control; warn is amber, danger is red. Focus: a 2 px ring of focus over a 1 px gap of focus-gap.",
    "ground": {"$value": "#000000"},
    "deep": {"$value": "#000000"},
    "column": {"$value": "#0D0E0D"},
    "well": {"$value": "#171917"},
    "raised": {"$value": "#232623"},
    "hover": {"$value": "#2F332F"},
    "text": {"$value": "#FFFFFF"},
    "dim": {"$value": "#BCC2BC"},
    "faint": {"$value": "#9BA29B"},
    "off": {"$value": "#5C615C"},
    "accent": {"$value": "#3DFF6A"},
    "on-accent": {"$value": "#000000"},
